        "comments": [
          {
            "author": "virtustom",
            "author_is_release_team": false,
            "content": "## FFe ##\n\n[Description]\n\nMerge Debian unstable 65.0-1 (upstream 65.0) as 65.0-1ubuntu1. stonking has 64.0-1ubuntu1 (FFe LP: #2165887).\n\nUpstream v64.0..v65.0 (91 commits), highlights:\n- mlx5: ConnectX-10 PCI IDs, clock and CQ cleanup fixes\n- rdma_topo: ConnectX-9 ID, multi-NIC and NUMA topology support\n- libibverbs: Completion Counters verbs, DMA-buf fd export for ibv_buf\n- librdmacm: repoll_* API, epoll in librspreload, CM event fixes\n- Provider updates: mana, efa, ionic, bnxt_re, erdma\n\nABI: no SONAME change, new symbols only. Private ABI bump (IBVERBS_PRIVATE_65) affects only libibverbs1 and ibverbs-providers from the same source, as in 64.0.\n\nUbuntu delta is unchanged: no pandoc and no man pages on i386.\n\n[Rationale]\n\n- NVIDIA GB300 Grace machines benefit from the mlx5 and rdma_topo updates.\n- Intel IPU E2000 (irdma GEN3) systems can benefit from the libibverbs updates.\n- Keeps 26.10 on the current upstream release, already in Debian, with no new delta.\n\n[Regression potential]\n\n- Consumers: ceph, dpdk, libfabric, openmpi, ucx, fio, libpcap, ...\n- No ABI break. Main risk is in mlx5/mlx4/mthca CQ handling and librdmacm event dispatch.\n- librspreload now also interposes epoll_*; this only affects apps run with LD_PRELOAD=librspreload.\n\n[Testing]\n\nPPA: ppa:virtustom/TODO\n- Builds: TODO (all arches; i386 exercises the man pages delta)\n- Reverse-dependency autopkgtests: TODO (same 14 sources as for 64.0, see autopkgtest-rdeps.txt)\n- Install and upgrade from 64.0-1ubuntu1 in stonking LXD: TODO (see install-upgrade.log)\n\nseeded-in-ubuntu rdma-core: TODO",
            "content_sha": "79305c8ba407dfdc90a6c12ab6aeb7e410405c722b9b536bc45233ee296d32da",
            "date_created": "2026-09-15T10:32:38.829040+00:00",
            "index": 0,
            "url": "https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/rdma-core/+bug/2167325/comments/0"
          },
